      "title": "Markdown Note: Usage",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "🔗 MiniMax H3 Image Conditioning\n\n### Name each picture and what it holds\nWrite \"<Picture 1>\", \"<Picture 2>\", \"<Picture 3>\" for the person, the coat and the trousers, bind each to a \"<Subject N>\", and describe the garment details to copy and what stays the same; casual wording such as \"the top from image 2\" simplifies the garment.\n\n### Keep width and height typed in\nThe person photo goes in at only 2 MP, so the output size is set here at about 16 MP; change it only for another shape.\n"
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "🔗 MiniMax H3 Image Conditioning\n\n### Name each picture and what it holds\nWrite \"<Picture 1>\", \"<Picture 2>\", \"<Picture 3>\" for the person, the coat and the trousers, bind each to a \"<Subject N>\", and describe the garment details to copy and what stays the same; casual wording such as \"the top from image 2\" simplifies the garment.\n\n### Keep width and height typed in\nThe person photo goes in at only 2 MP, so the output size is set here at about 16 MP; change it only for another shape.\n"
      },
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
    {
      "id": 1106,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        520,
        984
      ],
      "size": [
        400,
        170
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 8,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "Markdown Note: Usage",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "🔗 Load Image: person (image_1), Resize Image/Mask, Load Image: garment 1 and 2\n\n### Small pictures in, same quality out\nThe person photo is scaled to 2 MP and each garment picture to 1 MP: the edit runs about 2x faster (143.5 s down to 70.6 s on an RTX 5090) with the same face detail and garment fidelity at 1:1.\n"
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "🔗 Load Image: person (image_1), Resize Image/Mask, Load Image: garment 1 and 2\n\n### Small pictures in, same quality out\nThe person photo is scaled to 2 MP and each garment picture to 1 MP: the edit runs about 2x faster (143.5 s down to 70.6 s on an RTX 5090) with the same face detail and garment fidelity at 1:1.\n"
      },
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
